            "review_title": "Review at 4An Vegetarian",
            "review_text": "vargmanreturns\nPhu Quoc Island, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nHad high expectations- got disappointed\nJan 2020\nLooking for a vegetarian/vegan restaurant in Ho Chi Minh my girlfriend and I came across this nice looking restaurant. The staff was friendly and helpful, the menu looked really good. We ordered our food and two drinks- a bowl with tofu salad and brown rice with pineapple severed in a pineapple, a glass of carrot juice and a mixed glass(pineapple/orange). So far so good. When we received the food and drinks was when the disappointment began. The food we ordered, although very nice in taste, were really small. In one of them we found a black curly hair, we informed the waiter who gave us an apology and took the plate with the food in to the kitchen. He then returned with the same plate (without the hair in it) explaining that the black curly “hair” wasn’t hair but it was from the pineapple.\nWhen it came to the juices we were really disappointed. Again, nice in taste but my glass of mixed pineapple/orange juice was barely half full and my girlfriend received a glass with even less- about 1/4 of her glass. We asked why and the waiter response was simply “you ordered no ice”...\nA really disappointing experience and I would not recommend this restaurant. There are a whole bunch who are cheaper and with better service in this great city.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 31, 2020",
